Necessary allocation-sensitive count-variance cap
================================================
Mathematical status: locally derived, conditional on the original count
contract. No new physical premise, new target, or resource acquisition.

Write p=P(B=1), q=1-p and s=lambda/n. The sign-conditioned residuals have
means zero, variances w0=s(1-alpha)/q and w1=s*alpha/p, and supports in
[-O0,a0] and[-a1,O1], respectively. Reflect the first residual when
using the elementary pointwise inequality (U+a)(O-U)>=0, which gives
E U^2<=a*O for support[-a,O]. Reflection does not change the variance. Hence

  (lambda/n) [(1-alpha)/(q*O0)+alpha/(p*O1)]
       <= a0+a1 <= d0(1-lambda/Lambda).

O0 and O1 may be any valid positive contract upper bounds. Increasing
either only decreases the left-hand coefficient and preserves necessity.
All inequalities concern the same actual marginal and its same alpha.
Rearranging with positive n,d0,Lambda gives

  lambda <= [1/Lambda + f(p,alpha)/(n*d0)]^(-1),
  f(p,alpha)=(1-alpha)/((1-p)O0)+alpha/(p O1).

Find a lower bound c for f on the incoming closed p/alpha rectangle.
For each fixed p, f is affine in alpha, so its minimum over alpha is at
al or ah; equivalently minimum over the rectangle equals the smaller of
the two p-minima at these endpoints. For fixed alpha let
A=(1-alpha)/O0>=0, B=alpha/O1>=0. Then
f(p)=A/(1-p)+B/p is convex for0<p<1. Its derivative sign equals
A*p^2-B*(1-p)^2. If this sign is nonnegative at pl, the minimum is f(pl).
If it is nonpositive at pu, the minimum is f(pu). Otherwise the unique
stationary point lies inside, and the exact minimum is
A+B+2sqrt(A*B). The implementation replaces this square root by its exact
downward rational grid1e-12 approximation. Thus its coefficient c is at
most the true minimum, and the computed cap is at least every admissible
lambda. Degenerate alpha=0 or1 and degenerate p intervals are included.

Intersect only the current lambda hi with this cap; discard only if
incoming lo exceeds the new hi strictly. Equality is retained. The
original cfg.Lambda and every original price and plane stay unchanged.
All original count roots remain mandatory and leaf boxes are reconstructed
before this necessary contraction. The helper has no cfg argument and
cannot mutate the original intercept.

This is an arithmetic propagation of existing joint-plane/support premises.
It does not assert a stronger joint plane using the smaller scalar cap.
The final compositor must still acquire every original count premise.
